{"step_index":410,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:47:13Z","input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_tokens":58347,"output_tokens":1119,"content":"The **Critical Parsing Rules** and `clean_extracted_items` filter have been implemented across both the backend route and frontend extraction pipeline.\n\n### 🛡️ Implementation Summary\n\n1. **Item Cleaning Module ([`utils/clean_items.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py) & [`utils/itemCleaner.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/itemCleaner.js))**:\n   - **Header vs. Table Separation**: Enforces that header/footer metadata never becomes line items.\n   - **Exclusion Filters**:\n     - **GSTIN Detection**: Regex matching standard 15-character Indian GSTIN strings (`\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b`).\n     - **Phone Number Detection**: Regex matching 10-digit Indian phone/mobile numbers with optional `+91`.\n     - **Forbidden Metadata Labels**: Purges entries containing `gstin`, `gst no`, `contact`, `phone`, `mobile`, `tel`, `pan no`, `bank`, `ifsc`, `account no`, `invoice no`, `tax invoice`, etc.\n     - **Non-positive Filter**: Removes rows with quantity $\\le 0$ or rate $\\le 0$.\n\n2. **Gemini Extraction Pipeline ([`utils/aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js))**:\n   - **System Instruction**: Injected `CRITICAL PARSING RULES` (Header vs Table Separation and Item Exclusion Rules) into `GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION`.\n   - **Post-Call Sanitization**: Calls `cleanExtractedItems(parsed.items)` immediately after parsing the Gemini JSON response before passing it down.\n\n3. **Client-Side Text/OCR Parser ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js))**:\n   - Cleans extracted table rows through `cleanExtractedItems(items)` before any subtotal, tax, or total recalculations.\n\n4. **App Controller ([`app.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/app.js))**:\n   - In `handleFileUpload()`, validates and cleans items prior to running the audit engine (`auditInvoice`) and recalculating totals.\n\n5. **Server Route ([`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py))**:\n   - Added `POST /api/process-invoice` and `POST /api/clean-items` routes applying `clean_extracted_items(response[\"items\"])` before calculating precision totals.\n\nThe local server is running on **http://localhost:3000**.","thinking":"Initial hypothesis confirmed: the item cleaner utility is correctly implemented, encompassing header/table separation and exclusion rules for GSTIN, phone numbers, and other forbidden keywords, alongside checks for zero/negative quantities and rates.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":411,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:51:34Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nYou are an invoice OCR parser for Indian GST tax invoices.\n\nMANDATORY RULES:\n1. SUPPLIER NAME:\n   - Extract ONLY the business trade name or company name (e.g., 'Modern Electrical & Hardware', 'Sharma Enterprises').\n   - NEVER include phone numbers, email addresses, or 'Phone: ...' in the supplier_name field.\n\n2. WHAT IS A LINE ITEM:\n   - An item MUST be an actual product, part, material, or service from the invoice's item table (e.g., 'LED Tube Light 20W', 'Basmati Rice 25kg').\n   - An item MUST have a valid product name, quantity > 0, unit rate > 0, and item total.\n\n3. ABSOLUTE FORBIDDEN LINE ITEMS (DO NOT EXTRACT THESE AS ITEMS):\n   - Street addresses, plots, industrial area names (e.g. 'Plot No...', 'Industrial Area', 'Main Bazaar', 'Sonipat').\n   - Buyer/Seller GSTIN or PAN strings (e.g. '06AAECM...', 'BZKPALZD...').\n   - Pincodes or telephone numbers.\n   - Amount in words (e.g. 'Thirteen Thousand Nine Hundred...').\n   - Bank account details, IFSC codes, payment terms.\n\nIf a line of text is not a physical item or billed service inside the central table, DISCARD IT. Do not guess.\n```\"\n\n\nAdd this cleaning function to the backend and run it on extracted_data immediately before sending it to the frontend:\"\n\nPython\nimport re\n\ndef sanitize_invoice_data(data: dict) -> dict:\n    # 1. Clean Supplier Name (Remove phone/email artifacts)\n    supplier = data.get(\"vendor_name\", \"\") or \"\"\n    supplier_cleaned = re.sub(r'(Phone|Mobile|Tel|Email|Mob)[\\s:]*[\\+\\d\\s\\w@\\.\\-]+', '', supplier, flags=re.IGNORECASE).strip()\n    data[\"vendor_name\"] = supplier_cleaned if supplier_cleaned else \"Supplier Name Unclear\"\n\n    # 2. Filter out non-items from the items list\n    filtered_items = []\n    \n    # Common address/metadata keywords that accidentally end up as descriptions\n    address_words = [\n        \"plot\", \"sector\", \"industrial area\", \"bazaar\", \"road\", \"street\", \n        \"haryana\", \"delhi\", \"gstin\", \"gtin\", \"state\", \"thirteen\", \"thousand\", \n        \"hundred\", \"only\", \"rupees\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"a/c\", \"ac no\", \"phone\"\n    ]\n\n    for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n        desc = (item.get(\"description\") or \"\").strip()\n        desc_lower = desc.lower()\n\n        # Reject if description matches address/words or is too short\n        if any(word in desc_lower for word in address_words) or len(desc) < 3:\n            continue\n\n        # Reject if total amount matches common pin codes (e.g. 131001) or is clearly corrupt\n        billed = float(item.get(\"total_amount\") or 0)\n        qty = float(item.get(\"quantity\") or 0)\n        rate = float(item.get(\"unit_rate\") or 0)\n\n        # Quantity and rate must be positive\n        if qty <= 0 or rate <= 0:\n            continue\n\n        # If billed total is astronomically different from qty * rate (like 42 * 14 = 588 vs 131001), skip\n        if billed > (qty * rate * 10) and billed > 100000:\n            continue\n\n        filtered_items.append(item)\n\n    data[\"items\"] = filtered_items\n    return data\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T22:21:34+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
