{"step_index":421,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:52:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T22:22:21+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T22:22:21+05:30\nShowing lines 7-60 of 280\n7: \n8: const GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `\n9: You are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n10: \n11: TASK:\n12: 1. Examine the provided document or image.\n13: 2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n14: 3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n15:    - Set is_valid_bill to false.\n16:    - Set rejection_reason explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n17:    - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n18: 4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n19:    - Set is_valid_bill to true.\n20:    - Extract the EXACT vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, date, and line items (description, qty, rate, amount) visible on the bill.\n21:    - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data or dummy items. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to unreadable_fields.\n22:    - Extract exact declared amounts; DO NOT fix math mistakes in the extraction.\n23: \n24: CRITICAL PARSING RULES:\n25: 1. HEADER VS TABLE SEPARATION:\n26:    - Metadata in the header or footer (Supplier Name, Address, Contact/Phone Number, GSTIN, PAN, Invoice Number, Date, Bank Details) MUST NEVER be extracted as line items.\n27:    - The items array MUST ONLY contain tangible goods, products, or billed services listed within the invoice's central itemized table.\n28: \n29: 2. EXCLUSION RULES FOR ITEMS:\n30:    - NEVER create a line item for a GSTIN (e.g., 15-character alphanumeric strings like '06AAECM4821F1ZX').\n31:    - NEVER create a line item for a Phone / Mobile / Contact Number.\n32:    - Every valid item MUST represent a product or service with a genuine unit quantity and unit price. If a row lacks a product description or represents invoice metadata, ignore it from items.\n33: \n34: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n35: {\n36:   \"is_valid_bill\": boolean,\n37:   \"rejection_reason\": string or null,\n38:   \"unreadable_fields\": [\"string\"],\n39:   \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n40:   \"vendor_address\": string or null,\n41:   \"gstin\": string or null,\n42:   \"invoice_no\": string or null,\n43:   \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\" or null,\n44:   \"items\": [\n45:     {\n46:       \"description\": string,\n47:       \"hsn\": string or null,\n48:       \"qty\": number,\n49:       \"rate\": number,\n50:       \"amount\": number,\n51:       \"is_blurry\": boolean\n52:     }\n53:   ],\n54:   \"subtotal\": number or null,\n55:   \"cgst\": number or null,\n56:   \"sgst\": number or null,\n57:   \"igst\": number or null,\n58:   \"total_declared\": number or null,\n59:   \"bank_details\": {\n60:     \"bank_name\": string or null,"}
{"step_index":422,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:52:21Z","input_tokens":2581,"cache_read_tokens":69086,"output_tokens":2755,"thinking":"The instruction set now defines the target as an Indian GST invoice parser. The focus is to extract the supplier name, adhering to strict rules. The extraction requires only the business or company name, excluding any contact information like phone numbers or email addresses.\n\n\nA line item is defined as a tangible product or service present in the invoice's item table, requiring a valid name, positive quantity, unit rate, and item total. Text lines not representing a physical item or service should be discarded. The task involves verifying the document's authenticity as a business invoice and then, if valid, extracting specific data points, including vendor name and line items. If it is not a bill, the process sets the is_valid_bill flag to false with a rejection reason.\n\n\nThe cleaning function aims to sanitize supplier names by removing contact information and filtering out invalid line items. Supplier names will be scrubbed of phone numbers, emails, and similar data. Invalid items are identified using keywords related to addresses and metadata. It also eliminates items with very short descriptions or total amounts that correspond to common pin codes.\n\n\nThe item cleaning function currently filters line items with zero or negative quantity or rate, and also filters extreme discrepancies between calculated and stated totals. Further refinement can be achieved by checking for variations in key names across different invoice formats; handling `total_amount` vs. `amount`, `quantity` vs. `qty`, and `unit_rate` vs. `rate` as potentially valid keys. These variations will be added to the input to improve flexibility. The `sanitize_invoice_data` function should be moved into the helper file for direct use, and the server code updated to use it before sending the results.\n\n\nThe item parsing logic now accommodates variations in key names like \"quantity\"/\"qty\", \"unit_rate\"/\"rate\", and \"total_amount\"/\"amount\" to handle different invoice formats. The code is updated to populate both variations of these keys, ensuring seamless compatibility. Also, the supplier name extraction code now handles aliases \"vendor_name\" and \"supplier_name\" and cleans it, providing a default value if unclear. This is all integrated, ensuring compatibility with the user's function.\n\n\nThe server now applies invoice data sanitization before returning results, addressing inconsistencies and cleaning the data prior to frontend display. Subtotal recalculation is added based on the cleaned item data to ensure accuracy. The frontend processing is being checked to identify where the invoice processing logic is handled.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":55,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/privacyMasker.js","StartLine":35}}]}
{"step_index":423,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:52:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T22:22:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T22:22:44+05:30\nShowing lines 35-54 of 54\n35: }\n36: \n37: /**\n38:  * Pre-processes any raw text or object to ensure sensitive financial identifiers\n39:  * are sanitized before UI display or downstream AI requests.\n40:  */\n41: export function sanitizeInvoiceData(rawInvoice) {\n42:   const sanitized = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(rawInvoice));\n43: \n44:   if (sanitized.bank_details) {\n45:     if (sanitized.bank_details.account_number) {\n46:       sanitized.bank_details.account_number = maskBankAccount(sanitized.bank_details.account_number);\n47:     }\n48:     if (sanitized.bank_details.ifsc) {\n49:       sanitized.bank_details.ifsc = maskIFSC(sanitized.bank_details.ifsc);\n50:     }\n51:   }\n52: \n53:   return sanitized;\n54: }"}
